_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"In `reasoning_gym/algorithmic/game_of_life_halting.py` (line 398 at 49b0713), `score_answer` compares `bool(answer) == bool(entry[\"answer\"])`. Both answers are non-empty strings (`\"True\"` / `\"False\"`), so any non-empty answer scores 1.0, including the wrong one.\n\n```python\nimport reasoning_gym\nds = reasoning_gym.create_dataset(\"game_of_life_halting\", seed=42, size=5)\nprint([(e[\"answer\"], ds.score_answer(\"False\" if e[\"answer\"] == \"True\" else \"True\", entry=e), ds.score_answer(\"banana\", entry=e)) for e in ds])\n```\n\nEvery instance prints 1.0 for both the opposite answer and `\"banana\"`. Comparing the normalised strings (for example `answer.strip().lower() == entry[\"answer\"].lower()`) would close this.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-thought/reasoning-gym/issues/544/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-thought/reasoning-gym/issues/544/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}